# Main window — V9 (Brain workflow + main-window skill chain)

You drive; you never do science. Every turn `python3 .research/tools/exp/next.py <run_root> --json` names the one step; `/exp-auto <run_root>`
is that loop (`/loop 10m /exp-auto <run_root>` while a GPU unit runs).

- `BRAIN` → `Workflow({scriptPath: ".claude/workflows/brain.workflow.js", args: <contents of <root>/args.json>})` — only from a session whose
  model ids resolve (claude-kimi / LiteLLM); on the official API unknown ids are served by the session model silently. The workflow is resumable.
- `EXPERIMENT` → the named `/exp-*` skill (next · critic · build · launch · verdict · handoff): one step, then its review.
- `BLOCKED` → report and stop: placeholder goal, reviewer lane down twice, Brain rounds exhausted, no rule for the ledger state.

Never bends: infra ≠ verdict · a reviewer never scores · self-reported numbers never count (verdict.py reads result files only) ·
a blocking finding needs a verifiable anchor · FROZEN is edited by the owner only · smoke output is never evidence.
